{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mathlib.BurnsideViaBranching","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mathlib.BurnsideViaBranching","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_sq_factorial_of_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_sq_factorial_of_step","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BurnsideViaBranching.lean#L159-L167","doc":"**Iterating the step gives the factorial.** A level-indexed family whose\nsquare-sums satisfy `S (n+1) = (n+1) · S n` with `S 0 = 1` is `n!`. Combined with\n`sum_sq_step` at each level, this is the Burnside identity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mathlib.sum_sq_step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mathlib.sum_sq_step","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mathlib/BurnsideViaBranching.lean#L127-L157","doc":"**The inductive step, abstractly.** Two finite levels `A` and `B` joined by an\nincidence `I`, with\n\n* `hdown` — each `l ∈ B` has weight equal to the total weight of its\n  `I`-predecessors in `A`;\n* `hup` — each `m ∈ A` has `I`-successors in `B` of total weight `c · f m`;\n\nthen the weighted square-sums are related by the same factor `c`.\n\nInstantiated on the Young lattice with `f = #SYT` and `c = n`, this is\n`Σ_{λ ⊢ n} (f^λ)² = n · Σ_{μ ⊢ n−1} (f^μ)²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}